			<div class="content" id="post-content-2952552">
									

<p>&quot;and at least one Foundation agent armed with a <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">net launcher</span> mock tranquilizer rifle&quot;</p>
<p>First thing in, along with the picture, and I'm almost immediately hooked. Most SCPs have containment procedures that of course make you think &quot;Why do we need <em>these</em> specific implements to contain this.&quot;, which can stir up a great number of emotions, and this immediately caught my eye as one of the better examples of how to perform this function. This is a <strong>great</strong> hook, in my opinion. What would necessitate changing from net launchers, which can actually work, to mock tranquilizer rifles?</p>
<p>It was very nice to me how it seemed to be wishy-washy about whether or not it wanted you to be afraid, or at least that's how it seemed to me. Most SCPs start you off with a sense of unease just by the nature of the site and the stuff you're reading, and very rapidly you can adjust - is this a funny skip? a sad skip? a scary skip? I wasn't sure which one of these I was going to get, which was one of the things that made me keep reading, and then when it wrapped up, I let out a nice little &quot;D'aww&quot;.</p>
<p>+1</p>

