														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2962829">
									

<p>Excerpted sentences and paragraphs below. It's just a few things that that really bothered me:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Click&nbsp;for&nbsp;nit-picking</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Wow,&nbsp;rioludoodle&nbsp;has&nbsp;way&nbsp;too&nbsp;much&nbsp;time&nbsp;on&nbsp;her&nbsp;hands</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3092-A instances are cotton-stuffed felt plush gorillas, possessive of no identifying tags or logos&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like &quot;possessive of&quot; should be &quot;possessing&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They are sapient, communicative, capable of sight, hearing, touch, and ambulation of all four limbs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a list of qualities, but you forgot the &quot;and&quot; that should go before &quot;capable&quot; &#8212; the secondary list from &quot;sight&quot; through &quot;ambulation&quot; is finished, but the first one isn't.</p>
<p>Paragraph blocks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3092-A instances are remarkably proficient&#8230; &#8230;attempt to breach containment, with limited <span style="text-decoration: underline;">success. However,</span> thus far, all SCP-3092-A activity appears to have been intended&#8230; &#8230;buckets or canisters of various liquids placed atop partially-opened doors.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The underlined part is where I think you could end a first paragraph and begin a second. One paragraph about the guerrilla strategies and cooperation, one about the silliness of their tactics.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3092-A instances can be ripped, torn, or otherwise damaged&#8230; &#8230;typically after a long period of exaggerated expressions of <span style="text-decoration: underline;">pain. However,</span> in cases less severe than complete incineration&#8230; &#8230;is interpreted by them as medical attention.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Same underlining thing here, in the last long paragraph of the description.</p>
<ul>
<li>Also, &quot;guerilla&quot; has more than one R. &quot;Guerrilla&quot; is the correct spelling.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>

